  "live_records": {
    "q-65338": {
      "dom_id": "step-q65338",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "Let $f(x,y,z)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}}}.$ Find the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4).$",
      "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(2,4,4)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the definition of $f,$ we have that $f(2,4,4)=\\frac{1}{6}.$ Computing the partial derivatives, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x} & =-\\frac{x}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{x}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{2}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{108}, \\\\ {f}_{y} & =-\\frac{y}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{y}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}, \\\\ {f}_{z} & =-\\frac{z}{{({x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2})}^{3/2}}\\,⇒\\,{f}_{z}(2,4,4)=-\\frac{4}{{({2}^{2}+{4}^{2}+{4}^{2})}^{3/2}}=-\\frac{1}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the gradient of the function at the point $(2,4,4)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(2,4,4) & =⟨{f}_{x}(2,4,4),{f}_{y}(2,4,4),{f}_{z}(2,4,4)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, the linear approximation of the function $f$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(2,4,4)+∇f(2,4,4)\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}+⟨-\\frac{1}{108},-\\frac{1}{54},-\\frac{1}{54}⟩\\cdot ⟨x-2,y-4,z-4⟩ \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{1}{108}(x-2)-\\frac{1}{54}(y-4)-\\frac{1}{54}(z-4) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{6}-\\frac{x}{108}+\\frac{1}{54}-\\frac{y}{54}+\\frac{4}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}+\\frac{4}{54} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{x}{108}-\\frac{y}{54}-\\frac{z}{54}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
