    "q-129665": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129665",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "Let $f(x,y,z)$ be a differentiable function such that\n\n$$\nf(1,-1,-1)=-1,\\,{f}_{x}(x,y,z)=2x,\\,{f}_{y}(x,y,z)=-2z,\\,{f}_{z}(x,y,z)=-2y.\n$$\n\nUsing a linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1),$ estimate the value of $f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03).$",
      "worked_solution": "The linear approximation of the function $f$ at the point $(a,b,c)$ is given by\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈f(a,b,c)+∇f(a,b,c)\\cdot ⟨x-a,y-b,z-c⟩.\n$$\n\nSo, the linear approximation of $f$ at the point $(1,-1,-1)$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x,y,z) & ≈f(1,-1,-1)+∇f(1,-1,-1)\\cdot ⟨x-1,y-(-1),z-(-1)⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{y}(1,-1,-1),{f}_{z}(1,-1,-1)⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find ${f}_{x}(1,-1,-1),$ ${f}_{y}(1,-1,-1)$ and ${f}_{z}(1,-1,-1),$ using the given partial derivatives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(1,-1,-1) & =2(1)=2 \\\\ {f}_{y}(1,-1,-1) & =-2(-1)=2 \\\\ {f}_{z}(1,-1,-1) & =-2(-1)=2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨x-1,y+1,z+1⟩.\n$$\n\nFinally, we can estimate $f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03)$ by evaluating the linear approximation at $x=1.01,y=-1.02$ and $z=-1.03,$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(1.01,-1.02,-1.03) & ≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨1.01-1,-1.02+1,-1.03+1⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+⟨2,2,2⟩\\cdot ⟨0.01,-0.02,-0.03⟩ \\\\  & ≈-1+2(0.01)+2(-0.02)+2(-0.03) \\\\  & ≈-1+0.02-0.04-0.06 \\\\  & ≈-1.08\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-129665-a",
